":644.0284162484376},"charspan":[0,3],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/28","text":"= 0"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Example 4.28. Let us use Proposition 4.26 and Corollary 4.27 to classify toric supervarieties with supertorus Q (1) n and underlying variety P n ∼ = X Σ for the complete fan whose rays are ρ i = R + x i for i = 1 , ..., n and ρ 0 = R + ( -x 1 -... -x n ).","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":543.926322731723,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":72.00000000000006,"r":523.2783955200002,"t":583.3382818484375},"charspan":[0,255],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/29","text":"Example 4.28. Let us use Proposition 4.26 and Corollary 4.27 to classify toric supervarieties with supertorus Q (1) n and underlying variety P n ∼ = X Σ for the complete fan whose rays are ρ i = R + x i for i = 1 , ..., n and ρ 0 = R + ( -x 1 -... -x n )."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"For i = 1 , ..., n , the ray ρ i must be decorated by a subspace V ρ i such that [ V ρ i , V ρ i ] ⊆ C x i . Hence V ρ i = C θ i or 0. Likewise, unless V ρ 0 = 0, we have V ρ 0 = C ( θ 1 ± θ 2 ± ... ± θ n ) for some 2 n -1 choices of ± .","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":503.115467227112,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":72.0,"r":523.27575456,"t":541.4594162484376},"charspan":[0,237],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/30","text":"For i = 1 , ..., n , the ray ρ i must be decorated by a subspace V ρ i such that [ V ρ i , V ρ i ] ⊆ C x i . Hence V ρ i = C θ i or 0. Likewise, unless V ρ 0 = 0, we have V ρ 0 = C ( θ 1 ± θ 2 ± ... ± θ n ) for some 2 n -1 choices of ± ."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"It is straightforward to verify that condition (b) of the definition of a large-orbit decorated fan holds regardless of which subspaces are chosen. We therefore obtain a collection of 2 n (1+2 n -1 ) toric supervarieties which are not equivariantly isomorphic. Many, however, are isomorphic via toric morphisms (to be defined in the following section).","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":447.32446722711205,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":72.00000000000003,"r":523.2806400000001,"t":499.61641624843764},"charspan":[0,352],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/31","text":"It is straightforward to verify that condition (b) of the definition of a large-orbit decorated fan holds regardless of which subspaces are chosen. We therefore obtain a collection of 2 n (1+2 n -1 ) toric supervarieties which are not equivariantly isomorphic. Many, however, are isomorphic via toric morphisms (to be defined in the following section)."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Notice that if all but one of these decorations is nonzero, then the decorated fan describes a supervariety isomorphic to projective superspace P n | n . For instance, if V ρ i = C θ i and V ρ 0 = 0, then the coordinate superalgebras of the affine charts can be written as","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":403.7227409377749,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":71.99999999999994,"r":523.2790896000004,"t":443.8254162484377},"charspan":[0,272],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/32","text":"Notice that if all but one of these decorations is nonzero, then the decorated fan describes a supervariety isomorphic to projective superspace P n | n . For instance, if V ρ i = C θ i and V ρ 0 = 0, then the coordinate superalgebras of the affine charts can be written as"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"C [ t 1 , ..., t n , t 1 ξ 1 , ..., t n ξ n ]","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":384.321322731723,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":238.08399999999995,"r":357.1918144000001,"t":395.8024162484377},"charspan":[0,45],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/33","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"C [ t -1 i t 1 , ..., t -1 i , ..., t -1 i t n ξ 1 , ..., ξ i , ..., t -1 i t n ξ n ] .","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{